{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>This time I will praise YHWH.</b> This is the first of the thirteen attributes — it is the attribute of repentance. And therefore this Name is alluded to in his [Judah's] name, for he confessed and was not ashamed, and he caused Reuben to confess as well; and therefore there came forth from his seed David, peace be upon him, who established the order of repentance." "<b>And when.</b> When Leah had completed four sons and Rachel had no children at all, she was jealous of her with great jealousy, and she came to Jacob with the claim that he give her children by any means through the power of his prayer. He answered her that the matter is not in his hand and the withholding is not from him but from HaShem, may He be exalted. Then she gave him Bilhah her maidservant, so that she might draw the power of childbirth from herself through an act of thought. And this is what she said to him: ״הנה אמתי בלהה בא אליה״ — \"Behold my maid Bilhah, go in to her.\" And so Rachel said: I — there is in my name no letter ה\"י (hey-yod) that gives the power of childbirth, as there is in the name of Leah and in the name of Zilpah her maidservant; but in the name of Bilhah my maidservant there are two — בא אליה ותלד על ברכי׳ — \"go in to her and she shall bear upon my knees\" — by the power of the first one, ואבנה גם אנכי ממנה — \"and I too shall be built up from her\" — by the power of the second one. And she bore him a son and called his name Dan."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:26.016351606Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}